What about the commander of that white ship?

00:20:09.120 --> 00:20:10.780
To Iselon Fortress Commander-in-Chief,

00:20:10.900 --> 00:20:12.480
the expedition team has completed their mission.

00:20:12.500 --> 00:20:13.300
We ask for your guidance.

00:20:13.860 --> 00:20:18.890
We won't be able to make it this far.

00:20:19.470 --> 00:20:21.000
Looks like the bad luck is strong.

00:20:21.560 --> 00:20:23.170
Until when will that continue?

00:20:23.850 --> 00:20:29.760
Expedition team!

00:20:30.350 --> 00:20:35.090
Port left wing, 86618 to 97548, enter at once.

00:20:35.810 --> 00:20:36.370
Roger.

00:21:30.000 --> 00:21:54.680
I admit that I defeated the enemy in the Newnitzer.

00:21:56.760 --> 00:21:58.180
But I'm sure I was blessed by the weather.

00:22:00.030 --> 00:22:04.550
It was too much of a coincidence for Bukun and Yogni.

00:22:04.550 --> 00:22:07.870
In the space space where the original battle takes place,

00:22:07.870 --> 00:22:08.740
keep in mind that there should be no storms.

00:22:10.800 --> 00:22:13.500
Yes. In the place of the original battle,

00:22:13.920 --> 00:22:14.920
show the original battle.

00:22:15.780 --> 00:22:18.920
Well then.

00:22:22.890 --> 00:22:24.130
I won't blow the wind that turns the skirt anymore.

00:22:37.640 --> 00:22:39.600
I heard you're interested in skirts here, too.

00:22:39.680 --> 00:22:43.960
An excellent transfer student can be despised and bullied at any age and at any gymnasium.

00:22:45.640 --> 00:22:48.260
But I won't allow any insults to my sister.

00:22:48.440 --> 00:22:50.340
No, it's no big deal even if you're against stupid seniors.

00:23:10.520 --> 00:23:11.140
Who will win the next battle?

00:23:12.180 --> 00:23:13.250
The enemy or the allies?

00:23:13.490 --> 00:23:14.230
Here we go!

00:23:15.940 --> 00:23:17.860
This is the enemy's imperial army.

00:23:17.940 --> 00:23:19.850
This is our alliance army.

00:23:20.450 --> 00:23:21.190
I'll go this way.

00:23:21.270 --> 00:23:22.230
I'll go this way.

00:23:22.230 --> 00:23:22.550
Huh?

00:23:22.940 --> 00:23:24.500
The enemy won more than us.

00:23:24.800 --> 00:23:27.560
Are you guys going to die?

00:23:28.350 --> 00:23:29.270
No, Popran.

00:23:30.000 --> 00:23:31.000
I intend to survive as long as I can.

00:23:31.320 --> 00:23:33.630
And I'll keep the money to myself.

00:23:35.640 --> 00:23:37.620
If everyone wants to do that and no one dies,

00:23:37.740 --> 00:23:39.260
we'll win the next battle.

00:23:39.620 --> 00:23:43.180
Then I'll go this way.

00:23:44.700 --> 00:23:45.180
Hey!

00:23:45.940 --> 00:23:50.250
What are you doing?

00:23:50.590 --> 00:23:51.980
How about a bite?

00:23:52.640 --> 00:23:53.120
Hey!

00:23:53.260 --> 00:23:56.980
Will this be enough?

00:23:57.840 --> 00:23:58.320
What?

00:23:58.320 --> 00:23:58.920
How much?

00:24:00.000 --> 00:24:00.960
So which one do you want?

00:24:01.520 --> 00:24:03.050
I wonder which one.

00:24:04.700 --> 00:24:06.480
I have something to look into.

00:24:06.720 --> 00:24:11.390
What are you going to do with this?

00:24:11.570 --> 00:24:13.040
Put it where you think it will win.

00:24:15.000 --> 00:24:16.680
I'm confident in surviving.

00:24:17.420 --> 00:24:22.600
Hey, I don't know which one will win.

00:24:27.190 --> 00:24:29.170
It's just a cause of the sudden change of the weather.

00:24:30.000 --> 00:24:32.430
I don't think there was any mistake in the operation.

00:24:32.910 --> 00:24:37.750
I think we should continue the attack on Izeron Fortress in order to regain this formation.

00:24:38.590 --> 00:24:39.250
Hmm.

00:25:00.030 --> 00:25:01.390
You're studying war again?

00:25:01.650 --> 00:25:03.590
I'm in trouble.

00:25:03.950 --> 00:25:05.560
Even if I'm going to study history,

00:25:06.820 --> 00:25:09.620
human history is full of open pages and open pages.

00:25:10.420 --> 00:25:11.450
It's a mess.

00:25:12.010 --> 00:25:14.830
Even if you say it's war research, there's no way around it.

00:25:15.510 --> 00:25:24.520
In the end, the cause of the eruption on that planet was the weather.

00:25:25.640 --> 00:25:29.740
The winner of the battle is the ally of the heavens, Chinori.

00:25:30.090 --> 00:25:33.810
And because of Kamikaze, I forgot that the one fighting is a human.

00:25:34.970 --> 00:25:40.730
The one who decides the outcome of the battle is a human.

00:25:40.930 --> 00:25:44.310
That's right. And now, the enemy has the commander of that white battleship.

00:25:45.790 --> 00:25:47.610
Ah, ah. You're here again.

00:25:48.650 --> 00:25:55.680
Compared to the one girl who loves you, you're still the same, aren't you?

00:25:55.680 --> 00:25:57.050
Your letters of encouragement.

00:25:57.510 --> 00:25:59.870
The post is not free, it's God's.

00:26:00.000 --> 00:26:00.780
But it's a valuable resource.

00:26:01.060 --> 00:26:02.040
It's troublesome, isn't it?

00:26:02.080 --> 00:26:05.460
It's a pity to throw away a fan letter, so we can't finish it at the end of the year.

00:26:06.330 --> 00:26:06.850
That's fine.

00:26:07.730 --> 00:26:08.840
You don't have to say that.

00:26:09.320 --> 00:26:12.780
Anyway, it's the hero of the battle of El Facil seven years ago.

00:26:13.540 --> 00:26:14.270
What about you?

00:26:14.590 --> 00:26:16.710
For me, that battle was a failure.

00:26:16.990 --> 00:26:21.070
With only one victory, the Furukabu will suffer, and I won't be able to pay for it.

00:26:22.000 --> 00:26:23.960
Do you need a young hero for the alliance army?

00:26:24.780 --> 00:26:27.080
It's cheap for a publicity talent.

00:26:28.360 --> 00:26:29.970
Well, I'm...

00:26:30.000 --> 00:26:33.980
It's not a good war to work as a salaryman.

00:26:33.980 --> 00:26:36.130
It's not a good war?

00:26:36.730 --> 00:26:37.960
Don't say that.

00:26:38.120 --> 00:26:44.760
I've been thinking about how to win this war.

00:26:44.760 --> 00:26:48.460
It's a strategy that can't be taken up by a commander with a hard head.

00:26:48.940 --> 00:26:53.420
Send an order.

00:26:53.900 --> 00:26:57.860
Take the Konyu 1800 and send it to capture the Iselon Fortress.

00:27:00.640 --> 00:27:01.760
It's really not that bad.

00:27:02.100 --> 00:27:14.260
We have information about the enemy's deployment.

00:27:14.880 --> 00:27:18.320
The enemy is going to attack Izeron, Cairo, and Tiamat.

00:27:18.420 --> 00:27:20.810
The time of arrival is 0930.

00:27:21.090 --> 00:27:26.170
The Izeron medium-range forces will attack with all their forces.

00:27:26.870 --> 00:27:28.520
Destroy the enemy to the brim.

00:27:30.540 --> 00:27:32.860
You will be allowed to act freely in the fortress until the end of the year.

00:27:35.660 --> 00:27:37.410
I hope it will have a significant impact.

00:27:39.720 --> 00:27:44.700
The left wing of the guerrilla force will be entrusted to the expeditionary force of Reinhard von Musel.

00:27:49.230 --> 00:27:54.040
The left wing?

00:27:54.140 --> 00:27:55.420
The left wing?

00:27:55.580 --> 00:27:59.660
The left wing is the most important position in guerrilla warfare.

00:28:00.280 --> 00:28:01.740
If you're scared, you don't have to do it.

00:28:02.240 --> 00:28:06.240
No, if you order me to, I'll gladly accept it.

00:28:12.470 --> 00:28:14.000
Are you really going to leave it to me?

00:28:14.300 --> 00:28:16.250
I'm the one who decides whether the left wing is the most important.

00:28:35.920 --> 00:28:40.110
The battle that will be held at the 4th castle, Kiyomato, will be called the Fourth Kiyomato War.

00:28:41.690 --> 00:28:45.330
I hope that everyone will be able to participate in the battle.

00:28:45.490 --> 00:28:50.460
The name of the battle is also planned.

00:28:51.720 --> 00:28:53.820
Then, which one will win is also planned.

00:28:54.740 --> 00:28:55.860
Neither will win.

00:28:56.600 --> 00:28:59.520
The war has been going on for 150 years, and there is still a chance.

00:29:00.000 --> 00:29:06.560
It won't end with just one fight.

00:29:07.900 --> 00:29:09.000
This time, it's about the pain.

00:29:09.940 --> 00:29:11.420
It's like it's already planned.

00:29:12.100 --> 00:29:18.050
It's a planned action.

00:29:18.550 --> 00:29:19.300
It's not planned.

00:29:20.180 --> 00:29:23.040
It's about who of us will die.

00:29:23.790 --> 00:29:24.810
You can't tell just by looking at the schedule.

00:29:26.850 --> 00:29:28.370
So, if you have a plan to live today,

00:29:28.510 --> 00:29:29.550
Oh, that's a good woman!

00:29:32.220 --> 00:29:32.920
Let's go.

00:29:33.080 --> 00:29:34.220
But I...

00:29:34.220 --> 00:29:36.020
What are you talking about? You're still alive.

00:29:41.060 --> 00:29:52.660
They're all going to go out tomorrow.

00:29:53.050 --> 00:29:53.320
What?

00:29:55.620 --> 00:29:56.240
Let's go.

00:29:56.520 --> 00:29:57.890
Okay, okay.

00:30:15.870 --> 00:30:17.770
The most important thing is to protect the left wing, huh?

00:30:18.350 --> 00:30:18.970
That's really annoying.

00:30:19.710 --> 00:30:23.090
What do these fortresses think of Captain Musel?

00:30:23.970 --> 00:30:26.950
Most of them.

00:30:30.860 --> 00:30:37.900
Enemies and allies.

00:30:38.480 --> 00:30:47.420
Enemies are a shame.

00:30:47.860 --> 00:30:52.610
If it were him, he would do so.

00:30:52.850 --> 00:30:57.100
This is even.

00:30:57.400 --> 00:30:59.580
I have a match with you.

00:31:00.000 --> 00:31:00.780
Hahaha!

00:31:03.210 --> 00:31:06.310
The latest photo magazines are all about the emperor!

00:31:06.850 --> 00:31:07.910
The emperor's favorite!

00:31:08.490 --> 00:31:10.190
The new minister's sister!

00:31:10.490 --> 00:31:12.430
She's definitely a girl I like!

00:31:13.090 --> 00:31:16.980
Even though I'm the emperor, I'm not good at this.

00:31:16.980 --> 00:31:18.240
Ahem, ahem.

00:31:20.040 --> 00:31:22.940
Ahem, ahem. My brother is now the prime minister.

00:31:23.340 --> 00:31:26.480
The prime minister is not rich or powerful, but he's a millionaire.

00:31:27.220 --> 00:31:27.780
Hahaha!

00:31:28.580 --> 00:31:29.060
Do you want to do it?

00:31:29.240 --> 00:31:29.300
Let's go.

00:31:30.000 --> 00:31:32.690
If you have it, you'll be protected from the enemy.

00:31:34.340 --> 00:31:37.140
But is it really down here?

00:31:37.300 --> 00:31:37.560
What?

00:31:37.860 --> 00:31:39.950
That blonde Taisho-san.

00:31:40.370 --> 00:31:42.010
Idiot! That's a three-dimensional image.

00:31:42.230 --> 00:31:42.950
There's no way it's in there.

00:31:43.530 --> 00:31:45.430
I know, but I want to peek.

00:31:46.210 --> 00:31:51.520
What are you doing?

00:31:51.680 --> 00:31:52.550
Don't fight.

00:31:55.760 --> 00:31:57.500
Fight? What are you talking about?

00:31:58.170 --> 00:31:59.770
Our Taisho-sensei's honor.

00:32:00.000 --> 00:32:02.280
Are you the Koubun of Gaki Daisho?

00:32:03.360 --> 00:32:23.700
It seems to be our fleet.

00:32:24.160 --> 00:32:25.080
You can't leave them alone.

00:32:25.220 --> 00:32:26.440
They're eating the same food as us.

00:32:32.330 --> 00:32:32.610
That's enough!

00:32:32.830 --> 00:32:37.260
Please continue your performance.

00:32:37.640 --> 00:32:51.760
I'm Lieutenant Lieutenant Louis Helm and Lieutenant Wien Van Den Berghe.

00:32:52.100 --> 00:32:56.580
I'm Lieutenant Zeke Fried Kirchheis, directly under your command.

00:32:56.580 --> 00:32:58.540
I won't fight for nothing.

00:33:00.000 --> 00:33:01.940
Only tomorrow's enemy will be able to fight against us.

00:33:02.120 --> 00:33:04.060
Yes, but...

00:33:04.060 --> 00:33:04.460
Hm?

00:33:05.640 --> 00:33:07.160
Why is our name...

00:33:07.160 --> 00:33:10.970
We are only the first officer on the first floor, but...

00:33:10.970 --> 00:33:14.170
As long as you are a member of our fleet, there is nothing to be surprised about.

00:33:14.690 --> 00:33:16.140
Your name is also known by the commander-in-chief.

00:33:17.720 --> 00:33:19.510
The commander-in-chief?

00:33:19.630 --> 00:33:22.380
Even if you forget the name of the general of the other fleet,

00:33:22.820 --> 00:33:24.180
you will not forget the name of your own soldier.

00:33:25.100 --> 00:33:26.460
He is that kind of person.

00:33:26.700 --> 00:33:28.560
His name is Reinhard von Musel.

00:33:30.890 --> 00:33:32.590
He said we shouldn't fight for nothing.

00:33:33.490 --> 00:33:36.210
They're not that great of an opponent to fight for.

00:33:36.910 --> 00:33:41.960
That's good. That's why my fleet is strong.

00:33:42.020 --> 00:33:55.090
How's my soldier doing?

00:33:56.830 --> 00:33:57.800
Nothing special.

00:33:58.970 --> 00:33:59.350
I see.

00:34:02.270 --> 00:34:02.970
It's finally tomorrow.

00:34:03.880 --> 00:34:04.740
Yes, tomorrow.

00:35:18.240 --> 00:35:18.940
Move to the left wing.

00:35:19.300 --> 00:35:23.740
Move to the left wing?

00:35:23.740 --> 00:35:25.530
Move to the left wing fleet.

00:35:37.930 --> 00:35:39.730
Why don't you come out of the center?

00:35:41.230 --> 00:35:43.110
My fleet is the enemy's food until now.

00:35:43.130 --> 00:35:44.710
How will the enemy eat this food?

00:35:47.040 --> 00:35:49.340
After all, it seems that Gensui is going to sacrifice us.

00:35:50.060 --> 00:35:55.000
If he wants to do that, he has no choice but to deal with it.

00:35:55.420 --> 00:35:57.740
Keep moving forward as it is.

00:35:57.740 --> 00:35:59.870
But as it is.

00:36:00.000 --> 00:36:01.260
I'm just waiting for you to kill me.

00:36:02.120 --> 00:36:04.380
You seem to have an idea.

00:36:05.020 --> 00:36:07.080
Don't tell me you're going to do that?

00:36:07.540 --> 00:36:08.780
That's right. As expected of you.

00:36:09.100 --> 00:36:10.880
You seem to have noticed my plan.

00:36:11.300 --> 00:36:12.780
Isn't it too dangerous?

00:36:13.060 --> 00:36:14.550
I know it's dangerous.

00:36:14.870 --> 00:36:17.320
But is there any other way to save my fleet?

00:36:18.520 --> 00:36:18.960
Certainly.

00:36:25.720 --> 00:36:25.920
It's too late.

00:36:26.800 --> 00:36:28.540
It's okay.

00:36:28.760 --> 00:36:29.780
Leave it as it is.

00:36:30.000 --> 00:36:36.420
If you're going to die the same way, it'll be easier while you're asleep.

00:36:37.300 --> 00:36:45.160
We're moving forward even further.

00:36:45.220 --> 00:36:46.200
Distance, 16,000 feet.

00:36:46.300 --> 00:36:46.560
Are you stupid?

00:36:47.080 --> 00:36:48.260
Are you trying to be our bait?

00:36:49.420 --> 00:36:51.100
Or is this some kind of trap?

00:36:51.600 --> 00:36:54.520
Even if it's a trap, it's too wasteful to be a bait.

00:36:55.580 --> 00:36:58.100
That's the fleet that the commander of the white ship is commanding.

00:36:58.760 --> 00:36:59.280
Maybe...

00:36:59.280 --> 00:36:59.540
What?

00:37:01.120 --> 00:37:04.280
If that fleet is the bait, the Imperial Army is trying to get rid of the excellent personnel.

00:37:05.680 --> 00:37:07.510
What does that mean?

00:37:07.730 --> 00:37:11.180
It means that there are some messy, uncoordinated things going on in the Imperial Army as well.

00:37:11.740 --> 00:37:21.220
If we keep this up, we'll be committing suicide!

00:37:21.580 --> 00:37:23.210
Even if we know that, we can't go against the orders.

00:37:24.070 --> 00:37:27.000
Tch! The scouts at the fortress are not half-hearted!

00:37:28.430 --> 00:37:29.780
Then, at that time, we should have...

00:37:30.000 --> 00:37:30.560
I'll beat him to death.

00:37:30.820 --> 00:37:36.790
All of the allied forces, move forward.

00:37:37.230 --> 00:37:38.930
Focus on the enemy advance fleet.

00:37:39.350 --> 00:37:42.520
The enemy fleet will attack as soon as it gets close to the shooting range.

00:37:43.220 --> 00:37:44.860
Don't consider the damage to the fleet on the left and right.

00:37:46.720 --> 00:37:51.220
At this rate, both sides will be beheaded.

00:37:51.440 --> 00:37:52.920
It's certain to be completely destroyed.

00:37:53.340 --> 00:37:55.770
But he won't stop moving forward.

00:37:55.910 --> 00:37:57.190
What are you thinking?

00:38:42.440 --> 00:38:43.360
The fleet will enter the range.

00:38:44.130 --> 00:38:45.560
Prepare to attack.

00:38:46.720 --> 00:38:48.120
Now! Turn right at full speed!

00:38:49.290 --> 00:38:55.360
It's a

00:38:55.360 --> 00:38:55.820
It's here!

00:39:22.110 --> 00:39:22.530
What are you thinking?

00:39:22.930 --> 00:39:26.080
You're just saying that you're going to shoot me.

00:39:30.280 --> 00:39:31.870
This is a trap! There must be something!

00:39:32.330 --> 00:39:34.790
No, now! Attack now!

00:39:35.090 --> 00:39:37.240
What are you talking about? This is the enemy's hand!

00:39:37.680 --> 00:39:38.660
Attack after seeing the next hand!

00:39:39.630 --> 00:39:40.830
Then we won't make it in time!

00:39:41.960 --> 00:39:44.040
There is no need to speak on the battlefield! I am the commander!

00:39:44.860 --> 00:39:48.260
The enemy fleet has been deployed! It will be attached to the left side of our army!

00:40:00.000 --> 00:40:01.020
The fleet is moving to the left!

00:40:01.220 --> 00:40:02.540
We don't have time for that!

00:40:02.600 --> 00:40:02.860
What?

00:40:03.810 --> 00:40:05.800
The enemy's main force is right in front of us!

00:40:06.060 --> 00:40:06.280
Huh?

00:40:06.910 --> 00:40:14.380
The enemy's force is close!

00:40:17.030 --> 00:40:17.390
Commence the attack!

00:40:19.640 --> 00:40:20.160
Commence the attack!

00:40:50.760 --> 00:40:55.360
Look at the fleet that's supposed to be like this. It's the most advantageous position now.

00:40:55.360 --> 00:40:59.040
If this becomes a decoy, we're the main force, aren't we?

00:41:02.360 --> 00:41:04.380
But he is a brave man, Prime Minister.

00:41:04.860 --> 00:41:06.530
This is the last time.

00:41:06.710 --> 00:41:09.560
If we win this, we will never use this kind of Jado again.

00:41:16.520 --> 00:41:18.690
We will clash with the enemy army face-to-face.

00:41:19.070 --> 00:41:20.000
I know.

00:41:20.480 --> 00:41:21.730
It's already a battle of force.

00:41:21.910 --> 00:41:23.430
There's no other way but to win.

00:42:23.710 --> 00:42:26.160
Gaho's loss is 18,651.

00:42:26.760 --> 00:42:28.490
228,000 dead.

00:42:28.490 --> 00:42:29.660
The number of deaths is still the same.

00:42:31.090 --> 00:42:34.590
The problem is not the number of survivors, but the number of battleships that can fight.

00:42:34.610 --> 00:42:40.320
The consumption of battleships is now more advantageous for us, but the enemy army has an unharmed fleet.

00:42:40.820 --> 00:42:45.300
If that fleet starts attacking, we will not be able to avoid the annihilation of our army.

00:42:45.440 --> 00:42:47.100
Why didn't anyone attack when that fleet attacked us?

00:42:50.280 --> 00:42:56.850
Even if we can win by numbers, we have to calculate the number of that boy's fleet.

00:42:58.990 --> 00:42:59.550
But...

00:43:00.000 --> 00:43:03.900
What is that fleet trying to do for us?

00:43:05.116 --> 00:43:07.096
Relying on the fleet you once abandoned...

00:43:07.104 --> 00:43:08.904
It's not something that an Imperial soldier would do!

00:43:09.436 --> 00:43:13.676
So even if you win, you won't have to take responsibility for it.

00:43:14.492 --> 00:43:16.492
Soldiers should not be held responsible.

00:43:17.980 --> 00:43:20.440
I can't ask him for help now.

00:43:23.036 --> 00:43:25.596
Everything is decided by how we move.

00:43:25.660 --> 00:43:26.160
Yes.

00:43:26.716 --> 00:43:29.996
It would be unpleasant if the upper-class troops of the army were to be saved by me.

00:43:30.190 --> 00:43:34.720
I'm sure you understand, Reinhardt-sama.

00:43:35.120 --> 00:43:40.160
It's not enough to thank the 10 colonels and the hundreds of thousands of soldiers who were saved.

00:43:41.820 --> 00:43:44.860
Yes, that's right.

00:43:45.140 --> 00:43:48.430
The left-wing fleet, enter!

00:43:49.070 --> 00:43:51.980
Are you trying to save us?

00:43:52.440 --> 00:43:55.050
You're trying to steal the cavalry!

00:44:02.172 --> 00:44:04.352
There is no more time to waste!

00:44:04.668 --> 00:44:05.768
Do you have a plan?

00:44:07.612 --> 00:44:09.732
Go to the back of the enemy with a small number of ships.

00:44:10.236 --> 00:44:13.156
The enemy fortress is being attacked and in the meantime...

00:44:13.628 --> 00:44:15.168
The main body will retreat.

00:44:15.932 --> 00:44:17.172
It's a labor operation.

00:44:17.468 --> 00:44:21.188
But those who go to the fortress will probably never return.

00:44:21.756 --> 00:44:24.056
Who will take on that task?

00:44:26.588 --> 00:44:28.448
I'll do it.

00:44:31.120 --> 00:44:32.710
You are General Yang Wenli.

00:44:33.130 --> 00:44:36.220
What's wrong?

00:44:36.600 --> 00:44:37.960
You don't seem to be willing to help.

00:44:38.500 --> 00:44:39.940
Then why did you volunteer?

00:44:40.480 --> 00:44:43.010
You're just waiting to be annihilated even if you're here, aren't you?

00:44:43.110 --> 00:44:47.140
Even if you go to that world, your command will be a little better.

00:44:47.500 --> 00:44:49.010
That's a good point.

00:44:49.370 --> 00:44:51.170
I just want to make a little compromise.

00:44:52.050 --> 00:44:53.110
Compromise?

00:44:53.210 --> 00:44:57.000
If you had persuaded the commander even more strongly during the Regnitzer,

00:44:57.160 --> 00:44:58.530
you might have been able to live without making such a sacrifice.

00:45:00.440 --> 00:45:05.250
And if we had attacked that fleet on purpose earlier, it wouldn't have been such a terrible result.

00:45:07.720 --> 00:45:09.250
But, he's a commander with such a plan.

00:45:10.190 --> 00:45:11.500
Will he get caught up in such a strategy?

00:45:13.470 --> 00:45:15.410
I don't think I'll get caught up in it.

00:45:15.610 --> 00:45:17.870
But still, I think it's okay to try this strategy.

00:45:19.430 --> 00:45:24.740
I'll send out a mobilization unit led by General Yang Wenli.

00:45:25.180 --> 00:45:27.180
I pray for everyone's consideration.

00:45:28.980 --> 00:45:29.920
What? That's...

00:45:30.000 --> 00:45:30.160
Oh, really?

00:45:30.440 --> 00:45:31.520
What's wrong?

00:45:32.390 --> 00:45:32.610
Yes.

00:45:32.670 --> 00:45:35.810
All of them, but only three of them boarded the Commander Ulysses.

00:45:36.790 --> 00:45:38.090
The rest are all unmanned.

00:45:38.750 --> 00:45:40.090
Only three?

00:46:02.560 --> 00:46:03.160
I'm sorry, Captain.

00:46:03.760 --> 00:46:05.580
We should have been able to control this ship.

00:46:06.360 --> 00:46:08.240
This ship is a Jajau,

00:46:08.280 --> 00:46:11.390
so we can't leave it to you.

00:46:11.410 --> 00:46:13.620
Enemy airship, break through!

00:46:14.690 --> 00:46:14.970
Excellent.

00:46:15.430 --> 00:46:17.120
Now we just have to deal with them.

00:46:25.100 --> 00:46:26.200
Enemy fleet, respond!

00:46:26.380 --> 00:46:27.680
Eight thousand fleets are advancing to the fortress!

00:46:30.190 --> 00:46:32.550
Damn it! We can't go back to the fortress!

00:46:32.570 --> 00:46:35.280
We have to retreat and defend the fortress!

00:46:36.080 --> 00:46:37.800
The main force is retreating!

00:46:38.280 --> 00:46:40.200
We've been caught up in the enemy's sabotage.

00:46:41.260 --> 00:46:42.600
How foolish.

00:46:45.040 --> 00:46:46.480
The main force is retreating!

00:46:46.480 --> 00:46:48.240
You've been caught up, haven't you?

00:46:48.240 --> 00:46:50.000
All forces, attack the main force at once!

00:46:50.520 --> 00:46:50.880
Retreat while fighting!

00:46:52.180 --> 00:46:54.950
The problem is how long we can fool the enemy.

00:47:10.300 --> 00:47:13.080
The main force has been put on board.

00:47:13.160 --> 00:47:14.180
It's a mercenary operation.

00:47:14.560 --> 00:47:15.610
I can't let it go.

00:47:16.070 --> 00:47:17.210
Major Mittermeier.

00:47:17.490 --> 00:47:21.130
I don't need it, but please eliminate the ghosts.

00:47:21.930 --> 00:47:23.880
It's an enemy mercenary unit.

00:47:24.260 --> 00:47:26.880
There are already 12 high-speed battleships.

00:47:27.630 --> 00:47:29.480
Only 12?

00:47:30.730 --> 00:47:31.710
Do you need more than that?

00:47:31.830 --> 00:47:33.430
I'll take care of the enemy's mercenaries.

00:47:34.680 --> 00:47:35.120
Certainly.

00:47:35.980 --> 00:47:37.150
12 seats is enough.

00:47:37.470 --> 00:47:44.680
I'll take care of it.

00:47:44.760 --> 00:47:58.700
The enemy, the fortress, and the attack unit are the enemy's mercenaries.

00:48:00.060 --> 00:48:03.800
I see. Then do it thoroughly!

00:50:21.600 --> 00:50:22.930
It's a machine gun. The position is just below the turret.

00:50:23.740 --> 00:50:24.060
What?

00:50:24.360 --> 00:50:28.380
The machine gun doesn't attack.

00:50:28.780 --> 00:50:29.780
However, the enemy...

00:50:30.000 --> 00:50:32.380
If we attack now, the enemy's ships will be completely destroyed!

00:50:32.840 --> 00:50:34.820
Tch, you're such an idiot.

00:50:35.660 --> 00:50:38.130
Attack, Angel! Don't shoot anyone!

00:50:38.230 --> 00:50:40.880
Sir, now is the chance to attack!

00:50:41.700 --> 00:50:42.890
What are you talking about?

00:50:42.980 --> 00:50:44.200
Try attacking now!

00:50:44.320 --> 00:50:45.060
Even if we defeat the enemy's ships,

00:50:45.660 --> 00:50:47.860
the enemy ships that are burning in revenge will attack us!

00:50:49.380 --> 00:50:54.790
It's quiet. No one is attacking.

00:50:55.350 --> 00:50:56.700
It's important.

00:50:57.180 --> 00:50:59.150
We have to kill the people above us.

00:51:00.000 --> 00:51:13.130
If someone were to fire now...

00:51:13.130 --> 00:51:14.490
Then it would be hell.

00:51:14.910 --> 00:51:29.840
Kill Heize, I...

00:51:30.000 --> 00:51:33.020
We can't let our lives and this ship's victory go to waste.

00:51:33.100 --> 00:51:33.820
Please wait!

00:51:35.340 --> 00:51:35.640
Attack!

00:51:36.200 --> 00:51:41.520
Your Excellency, as far as this ship's actions are concerned, the commander-in-chief will be the commander-in-chief.

00:51:41.600 --> 00:51:46.470
As the commander-in-chief of the fleet, I would like to give you your responsibility.

00:51:52.720 --> 00:51:55.000
Warukai, the captain is right.

00:51:55.320 --> 00:51:57.620
The commander-in-chief of this ship is the captain.

00:51:58.120 --> 00:51:59.460
I won't let him get away with it again.

00:52:00.000 --> 00:52:03.260
I will proceed as it is.

00:52:03.580 --> 00:52:22.160
Retreat immediately!

00:52:33.260 --> 00:52:34.160
Alright, retreat!

00:52:34.730 --> 00:52:36.640
If we let the hostages escape, won't we get killed?

00:52:37.020 --> 00:52:38.640
I don't know either.

00:52:38.760 --> 00:52:41.380
But if I were the superior, I wouldn't do anything.

00:52:41.640 --> 00:52:43.480
This battle is over.

00:52:43.920 --> 00:52:45.900
The fourth Tiamat battle...

00:52:45.900 --> 00:52:55.800
Are you going to track them down?

00:52:55.840 --> 00:52:57.040
No need.

00:52:57.860 --> 00:52:59.200
Unnecessary tracking only increases damage.

00:53:00.000 --> 00:53:01.460
The battle is still ahead.

00:53:03.770 --> 00:53:04.670
It's over, isn't it?

00:53:04.670 --> 00:53:05.900
One battle is...

00:53:05.900 --> 00:53:08.030
Yeah, it's over.

00:53:08.250 --> 00:53:21.160
Did something happen?

00:53:21.860 --> 00:53:22.060
Nothing.

00:53:22.440 --> 00:53:25.730
It's just that you and I are lucky so far.

00:53:46.320 --> 00:53:47.740
Konef, you saved your life again.

00:53:47.980 --> 00:53:49.780
So, who won?

00:53:50.300 --> 00:53:51.390
I want you to win.

00:53:51.630 --> 00:53:54.360
Oh, since when did you wake up to patriotism?

00:53:54.700 --> 00:53:56.340
I'm not kidding. I don't want to lose to a bet.

00:54:04.540 --> 00:54:13.820
Not only did we save the imperial fleet, but we also made the enemy look at us from the other side and gave our army a perfect victory.

00:54:14.480 --> 00:54:19.720
This is something that deserves praise, and it is a war that we must continue no matter how many sacrifices we make.

00:54:21.510 --> 00:54:28.630
And the only thing that will defeat the invading army of a vicious war state is your devotion to your motherland.

00:54:30.000 --> 00:54:39.670
In order to protect the unity of the Republic of Japan, even if we have to give up our honor, it is the duty of the people, and you are the mirror of the people of democracy.

00:54:40.870 --> 00:54:47.040
As the head of the National Defense Department, I, Yobu Toriyunihito, am proud of you.

00:54:47.280 --> 00:54:50.080
He's really a man of bad luck.

00:54:51.260 --> 00:54:53.360
Is he just a man of luck?

00:54:53.660 --> 00:54:54.060
Huh?

00:54:54.430 --> 00:54:59.200
At the very least, that man is no longer a target in a skirt.

00:55:01.080 --> 00:55:03.780
He's a cheeky, blonde kid, but still...

00:55:06.110 --> 00:55:06.770
General Yan Wenli.

00:55:07.190 --> 00:55:10.020
I think I was a little off.

00:55:11.120 --> 00:55:13.310
How about a drink tonight?

00:55:14.620 --> 00:55:16.420
I just want to have a good cup of tea tonight.

00:55:16.820 --> 00:55:17.300
Alone.

00:55:18.140 --> 00:55:24.590
I found out about the commander of that battleship.

00:55:25.250 --> 00:55:28.060
General Yan Wenli.

00:55:28.500 --> 00:55:29.520
He used to be...

00:55:30.000 --> 00:55:31.260
He is called the hero of Erythrasil.

00:55:31.620 --> 00:55:35.250
It has become troublesome, Kirhi Ais.

00:55:35.460 --> 00:55:38.850
I have been thinking about only four things so far.

00:55:39.690 --> 00:55:42.500
One is what to do with this empire.

00:55:43.160 --> 00:55:45.430
The other is about my sister.

00:55:45.670 --> 00:55:47.560
And about my best friend.

00:55:49.250 --> 00:55:50.330
Furthermore, about the soldiers of my fleet.

00:55:51.330 --> 00:55:54.210
But one more thing.

00:55:54.250 --> 00:55:55.820
Something that cannot be ignored has appeared.

00:56:01.820 --> 00:56:04.420
What's the matter? Don't you like the tea I made for you?

00:56:04.940 --> 00:56:06.920
I found out the name of Mr. Yakko.

00:56:07.340 --> 00:56:09.010
Mr. Yakko?

00:56:09.230 --> 00:56:13.960
He's the commander of the white ship, Reinhard von Musel.

00:56:19.780 --> 00:56:22.170
Young Wendry Junshaw.

00:56:26.560 --> 00:56:29.180
Reinhard von Musel.

00:56:44.428 --> 00:56:45.068
This is...

00:56:45.580 --> 00:56:48.420
Among the heroes who shine like stardust...

00:56:48.940 --> 00:56:51.560
It's just the beginning of two small stars.

00:56:53.676 --> 00:56:55.596
The battle between the two heroes is...

00:56:56.076 --> 00:56:57.456
It starts here.
